Orthonym — Third-Party Vendored Artifacts
==========================================

This file records the provenance and licensing of third-party binary artifacts
shipped in this repository and invoked at runtime as unmodified standalone jars
via subprocess. Orthonym does NOT statically link, embed, or modify these jars;
its own source remains under the MIT License. However, two of the shipped jars
are shaded "fat jars" that bundle third-party components under copyleft licenses
(LGPL / GPL-with-Classpath-exception). Those components are redistributed here in
binary form, unmodified, and their license terms and source-availability
obligations travel with them — see each entry below. Their presence does not and
cannot relicense Orthonym's own MIT-licensed source, because they are invoked as
separate programs, not linked.


